# Deploy to AWS (ECS Fargate)

This project ships Terraform + a `dude iac …` command group that deploy the
ticketing system to AWS ECS Fargate. The full reference lives in
`iac/README.md` in the repo — this page is the short version.

## What gets provisioned

| Piece | Purpose |
| ----- | ------- |
| ECS Fargate ×5 | `frontend` (nginx, ALB target), `backend` (gunicorn), `websocket` (socketio), `worker`, `scheduler` — all from ONE image |
| ALB | Internet-facing entry point; HTTPS when a domain is configured |
| RDS MariaDB | The frappe database (master creds in Secrets Manager) |
| ElastiCache Redis | frappe's cache (`/0`) and queue + socketio (`/1`) brokers |
| EFS | The shared, durable `sites/` volume (site config, files, assets) |
| S3 + DynamoDB + ECR | Terraform remote state + the shared image registry (created once by `bootstrap`) |

One-off Fargate tasks (run by the CLI, never as services): **configurator**
(writes `common_site_config.json`, refreshes assets), **create-site**
(`bench new-site`, first deploy only) and **migrate** (`bench --site all migrate`).

## First deploy

```bash
dude iac login --env dev
dude iac bootstrap --state-bucket-prefix <your-org> --env dev --yes
dude iac init --env dev
dude iac apply --env dev
dude iac ship --env dev          # build + push + deploy the image
dude iac create-site --env dev   # first time only
dude iac status --env dev
```

The app URL is in `dude iac output --env dev` (`app_url`). Log in as
`Administrator` with the password stored in the `…/admin-password` secret.

## Everyday loop

```bash
dude iac ship --env dev          # after code changes
dude iac migrate --env dev       # after DocType/patch/fixture changes
dude iac logs --env dev --service backend --follow
```

## Where things are configured

- `iac/terraform/environments/<env>/terraform.tfvars` — region, sizing,
  `image_tag` (written by `deploy`), optional `domain_name` +
  `route53_zone_name` for HTTPS.
- `docker/Dockerfile.prod` — the production image (frappe{{#if withHelpdesk}} + Helpdesk{{/if}} +
  `apps/ticketing`). Add your own apps with extra `COPY` + `pip install -e`
  lines, mirroring `ticketing`.
- New environments: `dude iac new-env --env staging`.
